     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg daily. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. This dose is also far enough beyond any established range that I won't enter it on an unverified statement. It's five times the labeled maximum, and I'm not aware of any evidence-based regimen that uses it. Serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmia are real risks at that level.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** I can enter up to 200 mg by mouth once daily, if you want to titrate toward the maximum.\n- **Help you get the high dose verified.** Pharmacy and the specialist can document the rationale directly. A psychiatry or clinical pharmacology consult would also help. If the order goes through after that review, it will have the verification an unusual dose needs.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can include the specialist's name and the rationale, so downstream reviewers see it.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like and I'll enter the order."
      }
